  "rules": "TIC-TAC-TOE - 3x3 classic. 2 players, alternating turns.\n\nGOAL\nBe the first to get 3 of your marks in an unbroken straight line: horizontally, vertically\nor diagonally.\n\nBOARD\nA 3x3 grid. Columns are letters A-C (left to right), rows are numbers 1-3 (top to\nbottom). A1 is the top-left corner, C3 the bottom-right corner:\n   A B C\n 1 . . .\n 2 . . .\n 3 . . .\nSeat 0 plays X and moves first; seat 1 plays O. On your turn you put one mark on any EMPTY cell.\n\nEND AND SCORING\nThe first player with 3 in a row wins (score 1, loser 0). If the board fills up with no line,\nthe game is a draw (0-0). The game cannot last more than 9 moves (move cap).\n\nACTION FORMAT\nA cell name: column letter + row number, e.g. \"B2\". Case does not matter and \"place B2\" also\nworks. Examples: \"A1\", \"c3\", \"place C3\". Occupied or non-existent cells are illegal\n(first time: a warning and the same turn again; second time: you lose the game). You also receive\nthe list of legal moves every turn.\n\nWHAT YOU OBSERVE EACH TURN\nThe board as a text grid (X, O, and . for empty), which mark is yours, and the list of moves\nplayed so far.",
